-- For l4 batch: zero answers at once, and any other number counts up for
-- ever. Under a time limit, the row that never stops stops the batch, and
-- the row after it is not evaluated, even with --continue-on-error.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
countUp n MEANS countUp (n + 1)

@export default zero for zero, and never stops otherwise
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
answer n MEANS IF n EQUALS 0 THEN 0 ELSE countUp n
